# CoW 2G tuple-field ASSIGN silent no-op (PRE-EXISTING miscompile — filed gap).
# `lower_assign` / `lower_compound_assign` have NO TupleFieldAccess target arm:
# `t.0 = v` falls to `_ => // Other target types not yet supported` and the
# assignment is SILENTLY DISCARDED (a miscompile class per Core #8 — the
# language must either lower it or REJECT it at check time, never drop it).
# There is no in-body materialize to match, so the 2G loop fix does NOT cover
# the assign half (only the RECEIVER shape, `t.0.push()`, works — see
# cow_loop_bare_param_tuple_receiver.gg).
#
# Asserts the CORRECT output: private copy of the tuple, first field += 1 thrice
# → 13, caller stays 10. The compiler currently prints 10,10 (both writes lost).
void f((int, int) t):
    int i = 0
    while i < 3:
        t.0 = t.0 + 1
        i = i + 1
    print(t.0)

void main():
    (int, int) p = (10, 0)
    f(p)
    print(p.0)
